   "subject": "News about attributes",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Hi all,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">As all of you probably know, arrival attributes can be retrieved by defining functions with one argument. A very simple example:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248)\">traj &lt;- trajectory() %&gt;%\r\n  set_attribute(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;delay&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">3</span>) %&gt;%\r\n  timeout(<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>(attr) attr[<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;delay&quot;</span>])\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Then we implemented support for global attributes, making it necessary to add a second argument to retrieve this new set of attributes:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248)\">traj &lt;- trajectory() %&gt;%\r\n  set_attribute(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;delay&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">3</span>, global=<span>TRUE</span>) %&gt;%\r\n  timeout(<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>(attr, glb) glb[<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;delay&quot;</span>])\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">This method is a kind of rarity. It’s clunky, as it is not easy to document (and therefore to discover and learn), and non-scalable, because new features would require more and more additional arguments. Thus, it will be deprecated starting at version 3.6.3, which will be released at the end of this month.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">The new official method for retrieving attributes will be <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">get_attribute()</code>. It works in the same way as <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">now()</code> for the simulation time:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248)\">env &lt;- simmer()\r\n\r\ntraj &lt;- trajectory() %&gt;%\r\n  set_attribute(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;delay&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">3</span>) %&gt;%\r\n  timeout(<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>() get_attribute(env, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;delay&quot;</span>))\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">and for global attributes:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248)\">env &lt;- simmer()\r\n\r\ntraj &lt;- trajectory() %&gt;%\r\n  set_attribute(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;delay&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">3</span>, global=<span>TRUE</span>) %&gt;%\r\n  timeout(<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>() get_attribute(env, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;delay&quot;</span>, global=<span>TRUE</span>))\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">This is a little bit more verbose, but I believe it’s more consistent and intuitive. Moreover, it allows us to easily implement new features for extracting arrival information. In fact, <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">get_attribute()</code> will come hand in hand with two more verbs: <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">get_name()</code> and <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">get_prioritization()</code>, to retrieve the arrival name and prioritization values respectively.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">The old method will be still available throughout the 3.6.x series, showing a warning from 3.6.3 on, and will be removed in version 3.7.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Regards,<br>Iñaki</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGkgYWxsLDxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+QXMgYWxsIG9mIHlvdSBwcm9iYWJseSBrbm93LCBh\r\ncnJpdmFsIGF0dHJpYnV0ZXMgY2FuIGJlIHJldHJpZXZlZCBieSBkZWZpbmluZyBmdW5jdGlvbnMg\r\nd2l0aCBvbmUgYXJndW1lbnQuIEEgdmVyeSBzaW1wbGUgZXhhbXBsZTo8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48\r\nL2Rpdj48ZGl2PmBgYHI8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PjxkaXY+dHJhaiAmbHQ7LSB0cmFqZWN0b3J5KCkgJSZn\r\ndDslPC9kaXY+PGRpdj4mbmJzcDsgc2V0X2F0dHJpYnV0ZSgiZGVsYXkiLCAzKSAlJmd0OyU8L2Rp\r\ndj48ZGl2PiZuYnNwOyB0aW1lb3V0KGZ1bmN0aW9uKGF0dHIpIGF0dHJbImRlbGF5Il0pPC9kaXY+\r\nPC9kaXY+PGRpdj5gYGA8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PlRoZW4gd2UgaW1wbGVtZW50\r\nZWQgc3VwcG9ydCBmb3IgZ2xvYmFsIGF0dHJpYnV0ZXMsIG1ha2luZyBpdCBuZWNlc3NhcnkgdG8g\r\nYWRkIGEgc2Vjb25kIGFyZ3VtZW50IHRvIHJldHJpZXZlIHRoaXMgbmV3IHNldCBvZiBhdHRyaWJ1\r\ndGVzOjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGRpdj5gYGByPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48ZGl2PnRy\r\nYWogJmx0Oy0gdHJhamVjdG9yeSgpICUmZ3Q7JTwvZGl2PjxkaXY+Jm5ic3A7IHNldF9hdHRyaWJ1\r\ndGUoImRlbGF5IiwgMywgZ2xvYmFsPVRSVUUpICUmZ3Q7JTwvZGl2PjxkaXY+Jm5ic3A7IHRpbWVv\r\ndXQoZnVuY3Rpb24oYXR0ciwgZ2xiKSBnbGJbImRlbGF5Il0pPC9kaXY+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5gYGA8\r\nL2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PlRoaXMgbWV0aG9kIGlzIGEga2luZCBv